      "name": "MIASM (Minimum Information About Somatic Mutation)",
      "description": "A minimum-information metadata guideline for reporting cancer-related somatic variation data. Specifies required fields about the variant (gene name using HUGO, reference sequence accession), detection method, screened gene region, quality control and somatic origin assessment, study design and sample/tumor details (topography, morphology, source, number and geographic/hospital origin), and publication/source information; intended as a reporting standard for researchers, clinicians, database curators, and journals to enable data integration and interpretation."
